            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for a nail, then the Telugu for scissors."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: దువ్వెన",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దువ్వెన — duvvena — \"a comb\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దువ్వెన (duvvena) is native Dravidian. DEDR 689 lists duvvu, \"to comb\", and duvvena, \"a comb\", with Tamil uḻu, \"to arrange the hair\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
